# .gitignore for clouddbSEA
#
# Rename this file to ".gitignore" and place it at the root of
# C:\Dev\clouddbSEA\.
#
# Revised against the actual directory listing (2026-09-05) — corrects
# three things the first draft got wrong from CLAUDE.md notes alone:
#   - top-level dist/ exists and wasn't ignored
#   - top-level watchdog/ is a real (non-symlinked) folder, not just
#     referenced via build/watchdog-config.json
#   - sea-config.json / watchdog-sea-config.json are SEA build *recipe*
#     inputs, not build output — must stay tracked, not swept up by any
#     future broad ignore rule
#
# Still not fully verified against build/'s own contents (collapsed in the
# screenshot this was built from) — if build/ turns out to contain its own
# generated/ or config.json copies, the rules below already anticipate that,
# but double check with `git status` before your first commit regardless.

# Symlinked folders — real content lives in, and is already tracked by, the
# dev-tree repo (ark-cloud-storage-no-overflow). These are junctions/symlinks
# on disk; never commit their contents here, only in the one canonical repo.
/src/
/prisma/
/scripts/

# Compiled/generated output — regenerated by `npm run build` /
# `npm run prisma:generate` / the SEA build recipe in MySQLexecompileinst.md.
/dist/
/generated/
/build/dist/
/build/generated/

# Real, environment-specific config — may contain real cluster
# ClusterId/Secret pairs and DB credentials. Never commit; keep only
# config.json.example tracked as a template.
/config.json
/build/config.json

# watchdog/ itself is a real, manually-copied folder here (not symlinked —
# matches this project's established watchdog convention), so watchdog.js
# is fine to track as-is. Its watchdog-config.json is excluded because
# appDir is an absolute, environment-specific path per CLAUDE.md's own
# documentation of that field — not a secret, but not portable between
# machines either, so re-cloning this repo elsewhere shouldn't silently
# carry a stale path.
/watchdog/watchdog-config.json
/build/watchdog-config.json

# SEA build/packaging OUTPUT (the packaged exes, SEA blobs, bundled JS, and
# the watchdog's own runtime log) — regenerated by the build recipe in
# MySQLexecompileinst.md. NOTE: sea-config.json and watchdog-sea-config.json
# at the repo root are NOT output — they're the build recipe's own input
# config (same category as nest-cli.json/tsconfig*.json) and must stay
# tracked; only the *.blob/*.exe/bundle.js/log artifacts these configs
# produce are ignored below.
/build/bundle.js
/build/*.exe
/build/*.blob
/build/watchdog.log

# Dependencies — package.json/package-lock.json ARE tracked (needed to
# reproduce this tree's specific allowScripts approvals and dependency set,
# per CLAUDE.md's note that these are deliberately NOT symlinked from the
# dev-tree repo), but the installed node_modules itself is not.
/node_modules/
